[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 2. M2 native C++20 engine replacing Xyce on core analog

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: PLAN-V2-005
STATUS: InProgress
TITLE: M2a - C++20 linear core, SuiteSparse KLU and in-process NativeCppBackend
STATEMENT: >>>
Implement CSC sparse assembly with pre-bound device slots, SuiteSparse KLU shared-library adapter (real/complex, symbolic reuse), dense reference solver, linear primitives (R/C/L/K/V/I waveforms/E/F/G/H), OP/DC/AC/TRAN drivers, full spice_capi.h execution API, and in-process NativeCppBackend via LibraryImport/SafeHandle.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Phase: M2
Depends-on: PLAN-V2-001, PLAN-V2-002
Deliverables: cpp/linalg (SparseLu + DenseLu + KLU adapter), cpp/devices (R/C/L/K/V/I/E/F/G/H + waveforms), cpp/analysis (OP/DC sweep/AC/TRAN BE & Trap + UIC + breakpoints), cpp/audit (DC/AC/TRAN physical audits), cpp/capi, NativeCppBackend in Spice.Sdk (OP/AC/TRAN contiguous buffer marshaling).
Verification: GCC 12 and Clang 14 C++20 -Werror builds pass all CTest suites (1,000-node RC ladder ~29.6 ms GCC) AND .NET 11.0.100 NativeCppBackend passes live in-process OP/AC/TRAN tests against libspice_capi.so. Remaining to close M2a: vcpkg SuiteSparse KLU link test and head-to-head XyceBackend/ngspice SANDLER8/SANDLER9 comparison.
<<<
